{{also|Buono}}
==Italian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|it|la|bonus}}, from {{inh|it|itc-ola|duenos}}, later {{m|itc-ola|duonus}}, from {{inh|it|itc-pro|*dwenos}}, from {{der|it|ine-pro|*dew-||to show favor, revere}}. {{doublet|it|bonus}}, a later borrowing.

===Pronunciation===
* {{it-IPA|buòno}}
* {{audio|it|It-buono.ogg|Audio}}
* {{hyphenation|it|buò|no}}

===Adjective===
{{it-adj|buon}}

# [[good]]
#: {{ant|it|cattivo}}
# [[fair]]
#: {{syn|it|giusto}}

====Usage notes====
The [[apocopic]] form {{m|it|buon}} and (optionally) the contracted form {{m|it|buon'}} are used before masculine and feminine singular nouns, respectively, in the same manner as the indefinite article (i.e. {{m|it|buon giorno}}, {{m|it|[[buon]] [[amico]]}} but {{m|it|[[buono]] [[zio]]}}, {{m|it|[[buona]] [[sera]]}} but {{m|it|[[buon']][[amica]]}}, etc.).

